{title: He Calls His Own by Name}
{subtitle: John 10:1–18}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×20

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
At the gate of the sheep[Bb]fold in the [C]early light of [Dm]day
The gatekeeper o[Bb]pens and the [C]shepherd leads the [Dm]way
He calls his [F]own sheep by [C]name and leads them [Dm]out
And they [Bb]follow where he [C]goes, for they know his [Dm]voice
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am [F]the good shepherd
[C]The good shepherd lays [Dm]down his life for the sheep
I know my own and [F]my own know me
And I [C]lay down my life for the [Dm]sheep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The thief comes on[Bb]ly to steal [C]and kill and de[Dm]stroy
But the shepherd brings his [Bb]flock to pasture [C]and to [Dm]joy
When the [Bb]wolf comes [F]down the [C]hired hand will [Dm]run
But [Bb]the shepherd stands [C]his ground for every single [Dm]one
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am the [F]good shepherd
[C]The good shepherd lays [Dm]down his life for the sheep
I know my own and [F]my own know me
